{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795301034,"nonce":"PnWg9lljm5NvCHzPqMS7tbz/gYc=","title":"The markers of planes at the edge of the screen overlap","message":"**What happens.** The marker of a plane outside the view sticks to the edge of the screen. When two such planes lie in about the same direction, their labels (\"Bot 3 1962 m\", \"Bot 1 2225 m\") print over each other and over the bars of the display at the top left.\n\n**What should happen.** Markers at the edge stay apart, or merge into one marker with a count, and they never cover the display of the own plane.\n\n**Steps to reproduce.** Play `node play.ts solo` with four Veteran bots, and look at the top edge of the screenshots while the bots fly behind the player.\n\nAgent: Claude Opus 5.5","files":null}]}